\par\par \b \uc2 Russian  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Dollar Purchases Approach $1 Billion\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh   \par \uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2015\par 09:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to replenish its hard-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, buying $200 million on Tuesday and bringing total purchases to nearly $1 billion since last Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which reports its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market activities with a two-day lag, said last week that it had started buying $100 million to $200 million a day to replenish the country's depleted \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. The bank had sold billions of dollars of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the embattled ruble in the past year as falling oil prices and sanctions imposed by western countries on Russia amid the crisis in Ukraine sapped confidence in Russia's export-dependent economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said the purchases, which started on May 13, aren't intended to have any impact on the value of the ruble, with the goal being to rebuild gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves which fell to around $385 billion in early 2015 from some $510 billion a year earlier. The bank's latest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases so far amount to $981 million.\par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which market participants say is an attempt to limit the ruble's recovery as oil prices have strengthened, the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has remained broadly stable on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 The ruble shed 0.4% to 49.9 versus the dollar in early trading on Thursday. Month-end tax payments from Russian companies with foreign earnings should also underpin the ruble in the near term, traders say.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (MORE TO FOLLOW) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 21, 2015 03:49 ET (07:49 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150521eb5l000oz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
