\par\par \b \uc2 Ruble Hits Fresh Record Lows --Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh   \par \uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 03:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Russian ruble hit fresh record lows early Friday, pressured by a further drop in oil prices and the country's sluggish economic outlook.\par \par \uc2 The new rout in the ruble comes the day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed no commitment to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exchange rate. The Bank of Russia raised its key rate by 100 basis points, to 10.5% from 9.5%, which was less than what analysts had expected. It also said the ruble was undervalued by up to 20% even at current oil prices. The rate rise and comments did little to buoy the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ruble dropped to 57.0045 against the dollar in the first minutes of trade on the Moscow exchange Friday, taking its year-to-date decline to nearly 43%. The latest drop in the ruble came after Brent crude oil prices slid to $63.31 for the first time since September 2009.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro, the ruble touched a fresh low of 71 compared with levels of around 45 rubles per euro in December last year.\par \par \uc2 Recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  have also failed to reverse the downward trend of the ruble. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday it sold $206 million on Wednesday, bringing the overall amount of December \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to $5.48 billion.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  let the ruble float freely in early November, an essential step toward inflation-targeting, but it said it reserves the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when necessary for financial stability.\par \par \uc2 The falling ruble potentially offers some relief to the country's commodity-dependent and export-focused budget, but is seen as having an adverse impact on economic growth by fueling inflation, killing investment activity and denting household wealth.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 28, 2015 21:18 ET (02:18 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150301eb310003p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
