\par\par \b \uc2 Russian Ruble Sinks -- Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh in Moscow And Chiara Albanese in London   \par \uc2 866 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2015\par 18:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Russia's ruble Tuesday sank to its lowest levels since a run on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  mid-December, wounded by a fresh slump in oil prices and rising fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's emergency measures to rescue the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month aren't enough to staunch the crisis.\par \par \uc2 New selling pressure is possible before the end of the week, traders say, when Russian government officials are expecting rating firm \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  to downgrade \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's status to junk.\par \par \uc2 Having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly and raised the key interest rate to an already punishingly high 17 percent, analysts say the Russian government has few market mechanisms left to buttress the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last month, the government issued an informal mandate to exporters to buy rubles with their cash proceeds to stimulate demand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Now analysts say such purchases could be made a requirement.\par \par \uc2 More draconian measures are being discussed. With oil expected to fall further, "it's imperative for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain confidence in the ruble among households," said Per Hammarlund at SEB in London.\par \par \uc2 Officials are already divided over whether to impose capital controls, Russia's former finance minister, Alexei Kudrin, told a Russian newspaper earlier this week. Since the ruble began sliding this fall, the government has repeatedly denied that it plans such measures.\par \par \uc2 Both the Russian government and analysts say the ruble's fall is unavoidable, because it is largely tracking the downward trajectory in oil, Russia's main export, which was down 4% Tuesday, with international oil benchmark Brent trading at a nearly six-year low of $45.50 per barrel.\par \par \uc2 The ruble has fallen nearly 15% since the beginning of the year and hovered Tuesday at 65.6 against the dollar and at 77.2 against the euro near the end of trading in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 "The ruble is catching up now with the oil prices which went substantially lower during Russia's long holidays," said Denis Korshilov, head of fixed income, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and commodities at Citi in Moscow. "There is no reason for the Bank of Russia to play against the oil trend at the moment."\par \par \uc2 With the fall in oil and economic sanctions, \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is predicting an economic contraction of up to 5% this year. But analysts are more pessimistic, in December \uc2 Moody's\uc2  rating agency predicted shrinkage of 5.5%.\par \par \uc2 Oil's fall has steepened lately--it is down 20% since the beginning of the year--and that fall will drag Russia "even deeper into recession," said Bernd Berg, emerging-market strategist with \uc2 Soci\u233\'00\'E9t\u233\'00\'E9 G\u233\'00\'E9n\u233\'00\'E9rale\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Piotr Matys, rates strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 , said that with inflation accelerating in the coming months, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be unable to lower interest rates to stimulate economic growth. A wave of bankruptcies seems inevitable in the coming months, which will put pressure on Russian banks, he said.\par \par \uc2 A looming problem for the \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is controlling the fall so that ordinary Russians don't lose confidence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 So far, there was no jump in demand for foreign cash akin to last month as those who wanted to buy into dollars or euros have already done it before, said Pavel Stukanov, deputy head of the exchange department at midsize Moscow-based \uc2 Lanta Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In March, when Moscow annexed Ukraine's regions of Crimea and the first round of sanctions followed, households were one of the key drivers behind the ruble's weakness. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Russia\uc2  spent nearly $80 billion defending the ruble last year, so its reserves fell below $400 billion for the first time since 2009.\par \par \uc2 Russia's finance ministry\uc2  spent another $1.3 billion over Russia's 11-day New Year holidays, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 But with analysts predicting a further drop in Brent crude prices to $40 per barrel, the ruble could weaken to around 70-75 against the dollar, said SEB's Mr. Hammarlund.\par \par \uc2 He expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to impose formal requirements on exporters to repatriate dollar earning and broader steps affecting the Russian populace could follow. "A likely second step will be to limit the amount that households can exchange," he said. "A third step will be to increase the reserve requirements on banks' open \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions."\par \par \uc2 Concerns about sovereign rating downgrade also weigh on the Russian market. A cut to Russia's rating below investment grade is set to spark another selloff in the ruble, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Paul Rawkins, head of the emerging Europe sovereign ratings group at \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2 , said Tuesday that another spike in the ruble volatility, sustained low oil prices, faster depletion of the Russia's reserves and new sanctions are all factors that suggest a downgrade.\par \par \uc2 Fitch cut its credit ratings on Russia to the brink of junk late last week, saying the country's economic outlook has deteriorated significantly in the past six months amid sharp declines in oil prices and the ruble.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com and Chiara Albanese at chiara.albanese@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 13, 2015 12:40 ET (17:40 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150113eb1d002uv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
