\par\par \b \uc2 Ruble Extends Gains as Exporters Ordered to Sell Foreign  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  -- 3rd Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh   \par \uc2 889 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Dezember 2014\par 20:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The ruble extended its rebound, hitting the highest levels in two weeks Tuesday as Russian authorities ordered major state companies to sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilize the market.\par \par \uc2 The order, which applies to big exporters including \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  and Rosneft, is part of a package of stabilization measures that the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have imposed to pull the ruble back from the record lows set during last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. So far, the authorities have kept promises not to impose administrative controls on capital flows or ruble convertibility, sticking instead to less-formal steps.\par \par \uc2 In a sign of the country's rapidly worsening economic outlook, \uc2 Standard and Poor's\uc2  said Tuesday it is considering cutting Russia's credit rating to the "junk" category.\par \par \uc2 Citing "a rapid deterioration of Russia's monetary flexibility and the impact of the weakening economy on its financial system," \uc2 S&P\uc2  said it could lower the rating as soon as mid-January. A downgrade wouldn't have a major direct impact, since Russia is already largely cut off from western financial markets by sanctions, but it would be a symbolic blow that could set back the Kremlin's hopes of stabilizing the economy. A "junk" rating could lead some investors to sell Russian debt because they hold only investment-grade bonds.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and government officials met heads of Russia's largest companies last week to talk them into selling dollars and euros that they receive from exporting goods.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia said Tuesday it plans to hold "consultations" with exporters to find the best solution on how they will channel foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  into Russia's financial system.\par \par \uc2 "An even selling of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenues throughout the year is beneficial from the point of view of stability on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and from the point of few of hedging risks related to fluctuations in the ruble rate," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in an email to The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, First Deputy Prime Minister \uc2 Igor Shuvalov\uc2  said he told export-focused companies that Russia needs their dollars and euros as others sellers of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  left the market, making the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  the only seller.\par \par \uc2 Western sanctions have cut off Russian banks and companies from global capital markets, boosting domestic demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to repay debts, which along with a slide in oil prices sent the ruble to record lows this month. Many export-focused companies preferred to keep their funds in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the ruble didn't receive the usual support from monthly tax payments in November.\par \par \uc2 This week, the ruble was expected to win from another monthly round of tax duties that prompts exporters to sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to meet local liabilities. But the turnover of $2.5 billion in the dollar/ruble section by late afternoon in Moscow suggested that market players avoided any substantial action as the overall volume of deals normally exceeds $5 billion by this time of the day.\par \par \uc2 The ruble gained 1.7% to 54.85 against the dollar by 1347 GMT after earlier hitting its strongest level since Dec. 8 of 52.88.\par \par \uc2 This week the ruble, which has lost about 40% of its value against the dollar this year, also benefited from a recovery in Brent crude prices to above $60 a barrel. \uc2 Sberbank CIB\uc2 , an investment arm of Russia's largest lender, \uc2 Sberbank\uc2 , said in a note it expects the ruble to continue its recovery to 52 against the dollar this week.\par \par \uc2 The ruble's recovery has also been driven by the state \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . According to data released Tuesday by \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the finance ministry sold $920 million from its foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings last week to support the battered ruble.\par \par \uc2 The sales were the first since the finance ministry, which holds its funds at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said last week it would start selling its excessive holdings of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the "extremely undervalued" ruble. The finance ministry holds about $7 billion of foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves but hasn't said how much it would sell.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the finance ministry is separate from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales, which have exceeded $10 billion this month.\par \par \uc2 The impact of last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis reverberated through the economy even as the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regained some ground.\par \par \uc2 Banks across Russia reported a surge in depositors taking money out last week as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates to steady the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The crisis was a blow to the banking system, already weakened by Western sanctions and the souring economy.\par \par \uc2 Authorities scrambled to shore up the banks, with parliament approving laws in a single day to provide 1 trillion rubles in new capital, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  temporarily eased regulatory requirements.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 Access Investor Kit for \uc2 Gazprom OAO\par \par \uc2 Visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=RU0007661625"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=RU0007661625}}}\par \par \uc2 Access Investor Kit for Rosneft\par \par \uc2 Visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=RU000A0J2Q06"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=RU000A0J2Q06}}}\par \par \uc2 Access Investor Kit for \uc2 Gazprom OAO\par \par \uc2 Visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US3682872078"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US3682872078}}}\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 23, 2014 14:24 ET (19:24 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141223eacn002na\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
