\par\par \b \uc2 Russian Ruble Remains Volatile\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh   \par \uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2014\par 08:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Russian ruble was volatile in early trading Friday, amid continuing pressure from falling oil prices and another verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from financial authorities.\par \par \uc2 The ruble eased to 62.9 against the dollar in the first few minutes of trading on the Moscow exchange but then returned close to its Thursday closing level of 61.4.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become increasingly volatile since \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  let the ruble float last month. It has been hitting record lows on an almost daily basis as the price of oil, Russia's key export, plunged below $60 a barrel. The ruble selloff prompted authorities to step in with a combination of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and real action.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister, \uc2 Anton Siluanov\uc2 , said Friday that he sees no risk from selling excessive holdings of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the ruble is set to rebound in early 2015, Interfax news agency reported. So far this year the ruble has lost nearly 50% of its value against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week the \uc2 Russian finance ministry\uc2  said it was ready to sell as much as $7 billion to stabilize the ruble after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out massive monetary tightening, hiking its key interest rate to 17%.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed Friday that it hadn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday, making it the second day of no direct \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support for the ruble. Since the beginning of the month the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold around $10 billion in a bid to halt the ruble's rapid depreciation.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 19, 2014 02:38 ET (07:38 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141219eacj000s4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
