\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russian rouble slips as Putin speech fails to impress\b0\par\par\uc2 726 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2014\par 15:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to reflect reaction to Putin)\par \par \uc2 By Alexander Winning and Vladimir Abramov\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Dec 18 (Reuters) - The rouble edged lower against the dollar on Thursday, with traders saying President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  had offered few concrete measures at his end-of-year news conference to pull Russia out of a crisis.\par \par \uc2 The president said Russia's economy would inevitably rebound but provided no clear plan to tackle the crisis that has seen the rouble collapse around 45 percent against the dollar this year.\par \par \uc2 At 1355 GMT, the rouble was around 1.3 percent weaker against the dollar at 61.00 after opening more than 1 percent higher. The rouble was 0.1 percent stronger versus the euro at 75.05, after falling during Putin's speech.\par \par \uc2 Selling pressure on Thursday was less intense than earlier in the week which saw the rouble fall around 20 percent against the dollar at one stage on Tuesday, sparking fears of financial meltdown and posing a major challenge for Russia's leadership.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been hit this year by slumping oil prices and Western sanctions over Ukraine, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inability to prop it up -- despite two hefty interest rate hikes in the past week -- has raised fears Russia will have to resort to capital controls.\par \par \uc2 Putin, however, said Russia did not plan to order domestic exporters to sell their foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings - in what analysts say would be a form of capital controls - but urged his government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to work closely with them.\par \par \uc2 He reiterated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not "burn through" its reserves to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said the bank should have stopped its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  a long time ago. If it had, it would not have had to raise its key interest rate in an emergency move this week, he said.\par \par \uc2 "This point restricts the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the issue of carrying out \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, which could once more be used by market participants in the 'game' against the rouble," analysts at BCS brokerage said in a note.\par \par \uc2 The rouble fell around 10 percent on Monday, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hike its key interest rate by an unexpected 650 basis points early on Tuesday, though this provided little support.\par \par \uc2 By Thursday afternoon the rouble had lost 5 percent against the dollar this week, after a short-lived rebound on Wednesday when the finance ministry said it was selling \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a broad package of measures to support the banking sector and promised to make more foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  available via its repo auctions.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices, a crucial driver for Russia's export revenues, picked up on Thursday with Brent crude gaining more than 3 percent to over $63 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 Analysts see a probable pickup in exporter selling to meet end-of-month tax payments as a factor that could help the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to recover lost ground. The bulk of the monthly taxes fall due next week.\par \par \uc2 Fitch ratings agency said on Thursday the recent extreme rouble volatility and higher interest rates will deepen the severity of the recession in Russia next year.\par \par \uc2 SISTEMA SURGES\par \par \uc2 The rebound in the oil price helped Russian shares, which rose sharply on Thursday, reversing some of the heavy losses seen earlier in the week.\par \par \uc2 Business conglomerate Sistema jumped more than 100 percent after its chairman was freed from house arrest a day earlier and as Putin said he hoped Sistema would restore its position in the market.\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Yevtushenkov's arrest and the seizure by the state of one of Sistema's most valuable assets, its stake in oil company \uc2 Bashneft\uc2 , have dented business sentiment in Russia and caused a collapse in Sistema's share price.\par \par \uc2 The rouble-denominated MICEX index was up 6 percent at 1,492 points, while the dollar-denominated RTS rose 7 percent to 767 points.\par \par \uc2 Uralkali\uc2 , the world's largest potash producer, postponed the cancellation of 12.5 percent of its treasury shares on Thursday, in a move that was supposed to increase its free float to 38 percent from 33 percent. (Reporting by Lidia Kelly, Alexander Winning and Polina Devitt; Writing by Alexander Winning; Editing by Lidia Kelly and Susan Fenton) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-18T15:05:03.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141218eaci0076u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
