\par\par \b \uc2 Rouble collapse? Foreign "speculators" say it wasn't us\b0\par\par\uc2 By Karin Strohecker and Jemima Kelly   \par \uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2014\par 19:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 17 (Reuters) - A 20 percent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  drop in two days sounds like the opportunity of a lifetime for a savvy hedge fund superstar to earn a fortune. But foreign fund managers say they have mainly stayed away from bets against the rouble, because the Russian market is just too unpredictable and costly.\par \par \uc2 Dragged down by falling oil and Western sanctions over Moscow's involvement in the Ukraine crisis, the rouble has declined steadily against the dollar since June, culminating in a freefall this week.\par \par \uc2 Moscow has railed against foreign "speculators". But many of the people who might be proud to accept such a title say this time, they weren't to blame.\par \par \uc2 "It has just become too disorderly," said Paul Lambert, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Insight Investment who runs a $300 million \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund and exited his rouble positions about a month ago.\par \par \uc2 "You need to feel like you can get in and out, you need to feel like there is some kind of predictability. When something is in freefall, like oil prices are or the rouble is, it is very difficult to say: 'Today is the day, that enough is enough'."\par \par \uc2 Fund managers such as Lambert say it was local demand for dollars in Russia itself that broke the rouble, with Russian firms scrambling to buy hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay off loans, and ordinary Russians queuing up to buy dollars and consumer goods.\par \par \uc2 Russian companies needed to repay $45 billion in the last three months of the year. See graphic: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/nuk43w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/nuk43w}}}\par \par \uc2 Last week, state-run oil company Rosneft issued 625 billion roubles worth of bonds. It said the cash, then worth $11 billion, was for domestic projects and would not be sold to buy dollars, but many in the markets took it as a signal to sell.\par \par \uc2 EXPENSIVE, RISKY\par \par \uc2 Some foreign funds say they were kept away from shorting the rouble - borrowing roubles and selling them to place bets that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would fall - in part by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  threats to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market without warning.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still has reserves of more than $400 billion, perhaps not enough to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the long term, but certainly more than enough to crush anyone betting against the rouble on any given day.\par \par \uc2 "There is that quite strong fear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will step in quite aggressively, and that really prevents the build up of massive shorts...there is simply no massive position-taking either way," said Viktor Szabo, an emerging markets specialist at \uc2 Aberdeen Asset Management\uc2 , which has $525.9 billion under management worldwide.\par \par \uc2 Russia's soaring interest rates make the cost of borrowing in roubles to bet against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , known as the carry cost, high, whatever the outcome of the bet.\par \par \uc2 "If you want to short the rouble as a speculative investor you either have a very, very strong view and also perfect timing, or the negative carry is going to trash you before you have even started," said Cristian Maggio from \uc2 TD Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Speculative positions are very marginal compared to the overall demand for dollars," Maggio said. "It is real demand from domestic players that is pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaker and that makes it much more serious than it would be otherwise." (Reporting By Karin Strohecker; Editing by Peter Graff) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-17T19:46:40.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141217each00mgg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
