\par\par \b \uc2 Massive  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  May Folow  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2 's Hike- RenCap - -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,640 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2014\par 07:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0626 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--The Bank of Russia unexpectedly raised rates at around 0100 Moscow time (2100 GMT Monday) after the ruble hit all-time lows, staging its largest one-day drop versus the dollar since 1999. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its key rate to 17%, from 10.5%. "We would expect these measures to be followed by massive direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Renaissance Capital says. RenCap says an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level of about $20 billion before the end of the year could see the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gain by about 15%, assuming a stable oil price. (andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0624 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  is likely to leave its policy unchanged at its upcoming December summit, Nomura Securities says. BOJ Gov. Kuroda acknowledged the possibility of below-1% inflation in the near future, and thus, the weak inflation result is unlikely to lead to further easing this month, says analyst Yujiro Goto. "The latest BOJ Tankan [survey of business sentiment] suggests tightening in the labor market continues; Prime Minister Abe also mentioned that wages will definitely rise again in spring," he says, making it likely that the BOJ will keep its positive outlook on inflation. "Nonetheless, Kuroda's view on the latest drop in oil prices and inflation expectations could shift market expectations for a further BOJ easing, supporting USD/JPY." (bradford.frischkorn@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: TFD \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0614 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Thailand's economy isn't likely enjoying the full benefits of falling global oil prices due to the government's energy reforms, according to a research unit of Bangkok-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tisco Financial Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "A downswing in global oil prices will positively affect the trade balances of net oil importing countries including Thailand," says Tisco Economic Strategy Unit. "Our study shows that a 10% decline in the Dubai oil price will boost the current account by 0.13% of GDP, and thereby GDP growth by 0.17 percentage point." However, it notes that global oil price declines won't help lower inflation as much as it should, now that the Thai government "takes the opportunity to carry out energy price reforms by raising the Oil Fund levy on various types of petrol and the excise tax on diesel." (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: TAG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0612 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Malaysia may miss both fiscal and growth targets as global oil prices continue to plunge, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2 . It expects oil-related revenue to fall to 3.1% of GDP in 2015, below the government's forecast of 5.0% and this year's 5.9% figure. "We estimate total oil-related revenue coming in 40% lower with oil price staying at current levels" which would hurt the fiscal balance by 2% of GDP, BAML notes. Economic growth is forecast at 4.6% in 2015, vs the official forecast of 5%-6%, while the fiscal deficit in 2015 is likely to come in at 3.8% of GDP, above the government's 3% target. "Malaysia faces the risk of a double miss on both growth and fiscal deficit targets in 2015," it says. (jason.ng@wsj.com; Twitter: @ByJasonNg) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: TFD \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0527 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China needs more monetary easing and fiscal stimulus to put its economy on track to meet next year's GDP growth target, CLSA says. It says the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  is "behind the curve" on monetary easing as the ecoonomy continues to slow. It sees risks that China's economy will continue to weaken in December. CLSA expects another 0.50% to 0.60% interest-rate cut, though there is room to do more. The government may delay rate cuts to next year because of fears that it will encourage more leveraged buying in stock markets, it says. It also expects fiscal stimulus to pick up this month and in the first quarter next year. (jacky.wong@wsj.com; Twitter: @jackycwong) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: TFD \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0425 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Fears of spillover effect from Russia have pushed rupiah even lower Tuesday, after the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sank to a 16-year low Monday amid huge foreign outflows. Foreign investors have sold a total of 11.2 trillion rupiah ($909 million) of bonds in the first 12 days of this month, according to Nomura. "This rapid sell-off may have been caused by the spike in local inflation, broad selling pressures in emerging market assets and profit-taking into the calendar year-end," says Nomura. The bank says large foreign holdings of local government bonds, weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserve position and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's focus on current account deficit have also contributed to weakness in the rupiah. The rupiah falls 0.7% to 12,845 against the U.S. dollars Tuesday, after touching 12,695 Monday, the lowest level since the Asian financial crisis. (jacky.wong@wsj.com; Twitter: @jackycwong) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0424 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Hong Kong equities fall in the morning session after \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's preliminary China manufacturing PMI contracts for the first time since May, down to 49.5 in December from 50.0 in November. "The greater-than-expected decline in the flash PMI raises the possibility that December data will disappoint," says Nomura. "We expect more policy easing to help stabilize growth and to achieve the annual growth target of around 7.5% for 2014." The Hang Seng Index tumbles 1.4% to 22,702.48 as \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  (0005.HK) falls 2.1% to HK$72.55, extending declines for the past week of trading to 6.1%, while H-shares fare slightly better with the Shanghai Composite up 0.7%; the Hang Seng China Enterprises Index falls 1.1% to 11,094.31. (gregor.hunter@wsj.com; Twitter @gregorhunter) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0415 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The tumble in oil prices is triggering a rapid falloff in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of emerging economies and prompting short covering of the safe-haven JPY, but it's still premature to see parallels with the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crisis of 1997, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief market analyst Daisuke Karakama. Since then many central banks across the world have built up more ample foreign reserves and established swap accord frameworks, Karakama says. For many resource importers like Japan, oil price weakness is having a beneficial effect as they benefit from what is like a tax cut on crude. But the spotlight is now on the negative aspects of cheaper crude such as concerns about the shale gas industry in the U.S. and worries about the financial standing of energy exporting nations such as Russia. "The prevailing mood at the moment makes it difficult to consider risk-taking," Karakama says. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0404 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Global smartphone sales to end users jumped 20% in the third quarter this year compared to a year ago, research firm Gartner says, as prices fall and consumers increasingly make the switch to more sophisticated devices. Sales rose to 301 million units during the period this year, up from 250 million units during the third quarter of 2013, Gartner says. Eastern Europe, Africa and the Middle East saw their highest growth ever, with sales increasing by nearly 50% compared to a year earlier. (newley.purnell@wsj.com; Twitter: @Newley) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0400 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Japan's MOF sells Y2.7 trillion of 5-year bonds with a lowest price of 100.08 yielding 0.083%, a result largely in line with market expectations. While the latest issue carries a coupon of 0.1%, lower than 0.2% in the previous issue, traders have been expecting demand to come from overseas or from investors looking to use the bonds for collateral. The bid-to-cover ratio, a gauge of demand, improved to 4.24 from 3.70, while the tail, another indicator, stayed at 0.02, as in the last tender. Lead JGB futures were up 0.11 at 147.49 following the smooth auction outcome. (tatsuo.ito@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0400 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  decided yesterday that the rapid descent in the value of the baht against the U.S. dollar was a result of short-term factors, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spokesman tells reporters. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  started Monday at 32.80 baht per dollar and softened to 32.99 baht per dollar in the afternoon. The drop of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was due to a selloff in Thai shares by foreign institutional investors, causing the index to drop by 9.17% at one point, says Chirathep Senivongs Na Ayudhya. The selloff prompted non-resident investors to buy the U.S. dollars and other foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which hastened the weakening of the baht, Chirathep says. (warangkana.chomchuen@wsj.com; Twitter: @waanspeaking) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0359 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Malaysia's November consumer price index likely rose 2.7% from a year earlier, according to the median forecast of nine economists in a Wall Street Journal poll. This compares with October's 2.8% year-on-year increase. Economists say moderating domestic demand and soft global commodity prices helped to slow inflation. But consumer prices remained elevated after the government reduced fuel subsidies in October as part of its efforts to shrink its budget shortfall. "We noted softness in food prices and some other components of the CPI in October and feel some of that has likely continued through in November," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Australia & New Zealand Banking Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a note. The official data is due Wednesday at 0900 GMT. (jason.ng@wsj.com; Twitter: @ByJasonNg) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 16, 2014 01:26 ET (06:26 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141216eacg000um\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
