\par\par \b \uc2 Russian Ruble's Rout Continues\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh And Chiara Albanese   \par \uc2 425 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2014\par 15:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Russian ruble plunged against dollar on Monday, dropping to a new low below 60 before recovering slightly, even as a rally in oil prices promised some relief for Russia's faltering economy.\par \par \uc2 The ruble was changing hands at 61.25 against the dollar in late trading in Moscow, down more than 4% on the day, despite a rebound in Brent crude prices above $63 a barrel from an earlier low of $60.55.\par \par \uc2 The ruble's rebound after touching a early low mirrors a recent pattern which traders suspects reflects \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  laid low by falling oil prices which are a major blow for Russia's energy-export dependent economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have sold some $700 million in the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to a person close to the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not comment on its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reveals market activity with a two-day lag.\par \par \uc2 "There's no relief in sight, the mood on the market is pessimistic," said Igor Akinshin, a trader at \uc2 Alfa Bank\uc2 . "Any recovery in the ruble is used to buy into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Mr Akinshin said.\par \par \uc2 The ruble's continued weakness has continued even though the Bank of Russia continues to tighten monetary policy, raising interest rates for the fifth time in quick succession last week. Though the latest 100 basis point hike was broadly in line with analysts' expectations, some market players had expected more aggressive monetary tightening.\par \par \uc2 "The sell-off clearly accelerated in November and the ruble remains under severe selling pressure so far in December as well. In fact, December could prove the worst month for the ruble this year. In the meantime, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is clearly reluctant to use interest rates against the speculators," said Piotr Matys, rates strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 This item was corrected 1041 GMT because it misstated the ruble figure in the first paragraph. It was 60 not $60.\par \par \uc2 15 Dec 2014 10:54 ET  Correction to Russian Ruble's Rout Continues Story\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Russian ruble plunged against dollar on Monday, dropping to a new low below 60 before recovering slightly, even as a rally in oil prices promised some relief for Russia's faltering economy.\par \par \uc2 "Russian Ruble's Rout Continues," at 1417 GMT, misstated the figure in the first paragraph. It was 60 not $60.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 15, 2014 10:54 ET (15:54 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141215eacf0020b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
