\par\par \uc2 Top Stories\par \b \uc2 Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Russia Intervenes \highlight\uc2  Again\b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2014\par 12:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top News & Commentary\par \uc2 DJCOMM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, after the ruble fell to a fresh record low against the dollar in response to falling oil prices, market participants said.\par \par \uc2 The ruble dropped to 57.9860 against the dollar in early trade on the Moscow exchange, taking its year-to-date decline to more than 44%. The ruble soared to 55.94 in just two minutes around 0844 GMT, but then returned to levels of around 57.33.\par \par \uc2 "It looked like the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, causing a rapid move. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to put out the fire, but it is hard to withstand against the global oil trend with \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Dmitry Stadnik, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Rosbank, the Russian subsidiary of French \uc2 bank Soci\u233\'00\'E9t\u233\'00\'E9 G\u233\'00\'E9n\u233\'00\'E9rale\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia wasn't immediately able to comment. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officially discloses data on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  volumes with a lag of two business days. Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  details will be published on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's website on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The new rout in the ruble comes the day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed no commitment to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exchange rate. The Bank of Russia raised its key rate by 100 basis points, to 10.5% from 9.5%, which was less than what analysts had expected. It also said the ruble was undervalued by up to 20% even at current oil prices. The rate rise and comments did little to buoy the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The latest drop in the ruble comes after Brent crude oil prices slid to $63.31 for the first time since September 2009.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro, the ruble touched a fresh low of 71 compared with levels of around 45 rubles per euro in December last year.\par \par \uc2 Recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  have also failed to reverse the downward trend of the ruble. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday it sold $206 million on Wednesday, bringing the overall amount of December \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , before Friday, to $5.48 billion.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  let the ruble float freely in early November, an essential step toward inflation-targeting, but it said it reserves the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when necessary for financial stability.\par \par \uc2 The falling ruble potentially offers some relief to the country's commodity-dependent and export-focused budget, but is seen as having an adverse impact on economic growth by fueling inflation, killing investment activity and denting household wealth.\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCOMM1120141212eacc00iv4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
