\par\par \b \uc2 European Midday Briefing: Stocks, Ruble Sell Off as Oil Fall Further\b0\par\par\uc2 1,356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2014\par 12:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par European Markets: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European stocks sank Friday as energy shares continued to take blows from the oil-price slide, with the Stoxx Europe 600 on track for its sharpest weekly decline since 2012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Oil futures lost more ground after the \uc2 International Energy Agency\uc2  cut its 2015 forecast for global oil demand by 230,000 barrels per day, to 900,000 barrels a day. U.S. crude futures dipped below $59 a barrel, but later pared losses, while Brent crude was below $63 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 Traders "still do not know what to make of the continued decline in the oil price and whether it should be taken as a positive (pseudo tax cut for consumers) or a negative (a signal of economic slowdown)," said Richard Perry, market analyst at Hantec Markets, in a Friday update.\par \par \uc2 The Stoxx Europe 600 fell 1.5% to 334.38. It faces a 4.7% weekly decline, which would be its worst since March 2012, according to FactSet data.\par \par \uc2 The Stoxx Europe 600 oil and gas group lost 1.8%, with 31 of its 33 components moving lower. Oil major Total fell 1.6%, \uc2 Afren\uc2  lost 3.6%, and \uc2 Royal Dutch Shell\uc2  shed 2.1%. The group was looking at a nearly 8% fall for the week. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par American Markets Outlook: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stock futures pointed to a red open on Wall Street, as a further slump in oil prices continued to dampen the investment mood and fanned fears of an imminent stock-market correction.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Later in the day, reports on consumer sentiment and producer prices will be watched by investors, after surprisingly strong retail-sales data came in on Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Futures for the Dow Jones Industrial Average lost 103 points, or 0.6%, to 17,406, while those for the S&P 500 index slid 10.30 points, or 0.5%, to 2,013.70. Futures for the Nasdaq 100 gave up 34.75 points, or 0.8%, to 4,198.00.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nour Al-Hammoury, chief market strategist at ADS Securities, said the \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  could fall to as low as 2,000 if the index breaks below the current support level at 2,019.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Additionally, he noted that the gold/oil ratio - which he argued is negatively correlated with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Dow average - has spiked, suggesting that a "major correction in the global equities is under way, especially in S&P500." \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday, after the ruble fell to a fresh record low against the dollar in response to falling oil prices, market participants said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ruble dropped to 57.9860 against the dollar in early trade on the Moscow exchange, taking its year-to-date decline to more than 44%. The ruble soared to 55.94 in just two minutes around 0844 GMT, but then returned to levels of around 57.33.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It looked like the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market, causing a rapid move. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is trying to put out the fire, but it is hard to withstand against the global oil trend with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Dmitry Stadnik, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader at Rosbank, the Russian subsidiary of French \f28 \uc2 \f2 bank Soci\u233\'00\'E9t\u233\'00\'E9 G\u233\'00\'E9n\u233\'00\'E9rale\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Russia wasn't immediately able to comment. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officially discloses data on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volumes with a lag of two business days. Friday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  details will be published on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's website on Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Norway's krone hit a new five-year low against the euro and an 11-year low against the dollar as Brent crude slumped to $63 a barrel and West Texas Intermediate settled below $60--both five-year lows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the dollar stabilized against other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of Japan's general election on Sunday and as the focus among investors shifts to U.S. economic conditions and the Federal Open Market Committee meeting next week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market participants largely expect a victory for the Japanese ruling party, which would enable authorities there to continue their current economic programs that have sharply weakened the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . As such, if the result is as expected sharp market moves are unlikely, they say.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Instead, the focus is if and how Federal Reserve officials would signal a rate hike by dropping their assurance that rates will stay low for a !considerable time."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The dollar's rising trend will remain intact if the Fed removes the reference to 'considerable time,'" said Atsushi Hirano, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sales for Japan at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Royal Bank of Scotland\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =========================== \par Top Stories: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil Rout Continues After IEA Cuts Forecast\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil extended its slump, hitting levels not seen since the depth of the global recession in 2009, on fears about slowing global demand after the IEA cut its demand forecast.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IEA: Plunging Oil Prices Won't Dent Supply in Short Term\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Energy Agency\f28 \uc2 \f2  slashed its forecast for global oil demand growth for the fifth time in the last six months on Friday and said the current slide in prices won't dent global supply or hit demand, at least in the short term.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ruble Sinks Despite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market again to support the ruble after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell to fresh a record low against the dollar. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =========================== \par Insight & Analysis: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Creditors Seek Kiev Commitment Ahead of \f28 \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2  Visit\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Before the U.S., Europe and \f28 \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2  fork over billions of dollars more to help Ukraine plug a growing hole in its finances, they want to ensure they won't be throwing good money after bad.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Leaked: Warning To Banks Not To Leak U.K. Stress Test Results\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Leakers beware! British regulators are taking a zero-tolerance approach to any pre-announcements of next week's U.K. bank stress-test results. The U.K.'s Prudential Regulatory Authority has sent letters to banks warning them that any leaks of their, or any other banks', test results will not be tolerated, according to people familiar with the letter. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =========================== \par Still to Come: \par Friday, December 12, 2014 \par GMT                        Exp   Prev \par 1330 US  Nov  PPI \par               Final Demand-0.1% +0.2% \par               Ex-Food \par               & Energy    +0.1% +0.4% \par               Personal \par               Consumption       +0.3% \par 1330 CAN Oct  New motor vehicle sales \par 1500 US  Dec  Thomson Reuters/ \par               \f28 \uc2 \f2 University of Michigan\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par               Survey of Consumers \par               Sentiment Index Mid \par               Month           90 89.4 \par               Expectations Index \par               Mid Month          80.6 \par               Value (Current Period) \par               Mid Month           103 \par 1900 CAN      \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2  Weekly \par               Financial Statistics \par =========================== \par Other News: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece Again Beats Budget Goals\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece continued to beat its budget goals in the 11 months of the year, as restrained spending more than offset below-target revenue collection.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Eurozone Industrial Production Rose in October\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Factory output across the 18 countries that share the euro rose for the second straight month in October, albeit at a modest pace.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ukraine Premier Raises Risk of Default In Pressing for More Aid\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lawmakers gave initial approval to a government program containing the outline for an economic overhaul aimed at stabilizing the country's finances, as Western backers prepare a new aid package.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Danone\f28 \uc2 \f2  Committed to All Units\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Danone\f28 \uc2 \f2  said all four of its business units, including medical nutrition, play a crucial role in the group's quest to revive growth amid ongoing speculation that the French yogurt maker is looking at selling its smallest division.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Roche Names New \f28 \uc2 \f2 Genentech\f28 \uc2 \f2  Chief\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Roche said it plans to expand its board of directors by two members, as it announced the head of its important \f28 \uc2 \f2 Genentech\f28 \uc2 \f2  research and development arm will retire.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  Likely to Pay More than $1B to Settle Probes\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German lender \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  is said to be likely to pay more than $1 billion to U.S. authorities to resolve two probes examining whether it violated U.S. economic sanctions and money laundering laws.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Iran Talks to Resume Next Week\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nuclear talks between Iran and six major powers will resume in Geneva next week, \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to paul.larkins@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 12, 2014 06:47 ET (11:47 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141212eacc001jx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
