\par\par \b \uc2 U.K. Factory Output Points to Slow 4Q -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,679 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2014\par 10:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0933 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--U.K. factory output fell on the month in October due to weaker production of computer parts, chemicals and drugs, official data shows. Manufacturing output dipped 0.7% between September and October, although overall industrial production was down just 0.1%, buoyed by higher oil and gas production. The figures suggest U.K. factories are feeling the chill from feeble demand for British goods in the neighboring eurozone, and indicate the economy got off to a slow start in the final quarter of 2014. (jason.douglas@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 0929 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] --The Swiss average unemployment rate is likely to ease to 3.1% from a projected 3.2% this year with the country's economy showing a slight improvement heading into 2015, according to the head of the Swiss Labor Directorate. "We're seeing an improvement in the economy and with surprisingly strong growth in the third quarter we expect the average rate of unemployment to ease somewhat next year," says Boris Zuercher. The Swiss jobless rate rose to 3.2% in November from 3.1% in October, due largely to seasonal factors like the onset of winter and the scaling back of building sector activity, he said. (neil.maclucas@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0924 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Control Risks Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  is maintaining its medium rating for political and security risk for India, following the stability brought by the new Bharatiya Janata Party-led national government. However, it says the optimism would be tested in 2015 as "the new leaders struggle to overcome resistance to ambitious reform agenda." The political, security and integrity risk consultancy firm further adds: "Improvements from a foreign investor perspective will take longer to emerge, as entrenched challenges involving land, labour, corruption and bureaucracy persist. But long-term prospects have improved, and interest will be amplified as Chinese growth slows." (krishna.jai@wsj.com; Twitter: @jaikrishna) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0919 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] State-owned \f28 \uc2 \f2 PetroVietnam\f28 \uc2 \f2  won't likely cut its production despite the recent declines in world crude oil prices, a company official says. The company says it will likely produce 17.2 million metric tons of crude oil this year, 6.2% higher than its initial target. The company has so far this year produced 16.2 million metric tons of crude oil, it says. This includes 14.4 million tons from domestic fields and the remainder from overseas fields. \f28 \uc2 \f2 PetroVietnam\f28 \uc2 \f2  says it is expected to produce 10 billion cubic meters of gas this year, 5.3% higher than its initial target. (trong-khanh.vu@wsj.com; Twitter: @TrongKhanhVu) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0917 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Economic growth disappointed in the third quarter and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chose to keep interest-rates high this month, but Indian consumers remain convinced that better times are ahead. ZyFin Research's Economic Conditions index hit an all-time high in November, having increased gradually over the course of this year. The index, based on a survey of 3,000 consumers in 11 cities across the country, was created in October 2011 and moved steadily downward until a year ago, when expectations began building that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Narendra Modi\f28 \uc2 \f2  would become India's next prime minister. That prediction bore out, and since then, investors and consumers have been upbeat about future growth despite concerns that Modi's economic policies have so far failed to revive investment. (raymond.zhong@wsj.com; Twitter: @zhonggg) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0917 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Bad news surrounding the Russian economy continues to mount. The price of oil heads south again, falling to five-year lows, and this has prompted the \f28 \uc2 \f2 World Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  to downgrade its forecasts for Russia's GDP growth. It now sees Russia's GDP falling 0.7% in 2015, from a previous flat forecast, an cuts 2016 GDP growth forecast to +0.3% from +0.4%. The ruble remains under pressure, trading at 54.18 against the dollar, despite hefty moves from the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support it. On Friday, the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  carried out its largest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this month to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the bank's data showed Tuesday. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold $1.926 billion in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on Friday, taking the overall amount of December \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to $4.53 billion. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reveals \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data with a lag of two trading days. (peter.nurse@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0911 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Thailand's military-appointed government is rolling out special financial measures as New Year gifts for low-income earners and SME operators. Finance Minister Sommai Phasee says that measures approved by the cabinet--that will come into effect at the beginning of 2015--include a nano-finance loan program, corporate tax incentives and import tax cuts for raw materials for SME businesses and high-interest savings bonds for the public. Tax-related measures are expected to cost the state coffer around eight billion baht ($243 million) per year while the government has allocated 100 billion baht ($3.03 billion) for the bond program, according to Sommai. (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0906 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The number of employed foreign workers in Spain has dropped 17% to 1.5 million, or 9% of all employed in the country, according to a report released Tuesday by Ramstad. The number of foreign construction workers is down 50%, with workers in farm activities down 36%. Asian foreign workers--mostly Chinese, a community with virtually zero unemployment--are the only ones whose number increased in the period, up 13% to 173,518. Ramstad also notes that its data is very much in synch with overall population shifts towards the coastal areas in a country that is emptying in the middle: the number of foreign workers decreased most in landlocked regions such as Castilla-La Mancha, Extremadura and La Rioja. (david.roman@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0905 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] India's current account deficit should remain comfortably financed, says Mole Hau from the economic desk of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The deficit in the three months ended September 30 nearly doubled to $10.1 billion, from $5.2 billion in the same period last year and $7.8 billion in the preceding quarter, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data show. "Gold imports were a key behind the widening but underlying data also showed signs of domestic demand revival," Hau says in a note. In the near term, the sharp fall in crude oil prices is likely to more than negate the impact of higher gold imports. \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects the deficit for a second year in a row to be below the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 's "sustainably financed" (BNP's words) level of 2.5% of gross domestic product. (nupur.acharya@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0858 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The Austrian economy might slip into a recession in the fourth quarter, the country's main economic forecaster, known by its German acronym WIFO, says Tuesday. WIFO also revises down the Alpine country's 3Q gross domestic product calculations. Whereas it previously said the economy had stagnated in the 3Q, WIFO now says 3Q GDP shrank 0.1% in comparison to both the previous quarter and the 3Q a year ago. This is the first quarter of negative growth since the beginning of 2013, when 1Q 2013 GDP shrank 0.1% on the quarter and shrank 0.5% on an annual basis. Leading indicators don't give much hope for an upswing in the 4Q and the possibility of a recession can't be excluded, WIFO says. The 3Q 2014 economic slump was in part because of a decrease in exports, WIFO says. Private consumption also only grew 0.1% on the quarter. (Nicole.lundeen@wsj.com, @nicole_lundeen) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0855 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Czech price growth in commodities such as oil and foods slowed in November, but domestic demand remains well anchored and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely won't be very concerned about the Nov. deceleration in CPI, says Radomir Jac, chief economist at Generali PPF Asset Management. "Demand in the Czech economy remains solid...and the Czech economy is not facing a threat of deflation from this point of view," Mr. Jac says. Excluding commodities, other items on the inflation basket are running ahead of the headline figure and that should continue, he says. However "oil prices will represent downside risk for the inflation outlook in the months to come," Mr. Jac says. (sean.carney@wsj.com, @SeanCarneyWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0844 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/TWD is little changed, as exporter sales offset foreign investor buying, say two local traders. The pair closes at 31.290--its highest onshore closing level in over 50 months, versus 31.285 late Monday; they say the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is believed to have bought the U.S. dollar around 31.210 (versus 31.200 Monday) to keep the pair in its target band. The USD/TWD stayed below 31.200 in the early morning due to a weaker USD/JPY, but sharp gains in the USD/CNY then triggered buying from importers and foreign investors and lifted the USD/TWD. "With Chinese yuan deviating from the rising Korean won and Japanese yen, it was hard to find a clear direction for the Taiwan dollar," a trader says. Taiwan shares end 0.6% lower Tuesday; foreign investors have been net sellers of local stocks for three straight sessions. (fanny.liu@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 09, 2014 04:33 ET (09:33 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141209eac9000yu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex