\par\par \b \uc2 The  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  of the Russian Federation\uc2  (Bank of Russia)-On situation in  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  market and  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  repos\b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2014\par \uc2 ENP Newswire\par \uc2 ENPNEW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014, Electronic News Publishing. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 Release date - 04122014\par \par \uc2 In order to stabilise the situation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  held \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and decided to set from 4 December 2014 the minimum interest rates on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  repos for all terms (one-week, 28-day, and 12-month) equal to LIBOR rates in corresponding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and for comparable terms plus 0.5 percentage points.\par \par \uc2 According to Bank of Russia estimates, the current ruble exchange rate has deviated considerably from fundamentally reasonable values, i.e. the level determined by the impact of macroeconomic factors primarily affecting the balance of payments: export prices, interest rate differential, economic activity and other parameters. Currently observed dynamics of the ruble exchange rate, including its redundant volatility, create prerequisites for financial stability risks, and stable depreciation and inflation expectations.\par \par \uc2 The measures taken by the Bank of Russia will facilitate the return of the exchange rate to the fundamentally reasonable values. Decrease in the interest rates on \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity will enhance their effectiveness and balance supply and demand in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with lower volatility of the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia will continue to follow the situation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and analyse its impact on other segments of the financial market and the behaviour of the economic agents. If required, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is determined to carry out further unlimited \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  without prior notice. The information on the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be published in accordance with the established procedure.\par \par \uc2 On 11 December 2014, the meeting of the Bank of Russia Board of Directors will consider the key rate level and provide a detailed analysis of the economic conditions and an updated forecast.\par \par \uc2 [Editorial queries for this story should be sent to newswire@enpublishing.co.uk]\par \par \uc2 Dokument ENPNEW0020141205eac5000k9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
