\par\par \b \uc2 How Low Can Ruble Go? -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dimitra DeFotis  \par \uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2014\par 00:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the ruble this week may have a short-lived effect, the Wall Street Journal reports.\par \par \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to a free float of the ruble Nov. 10. But the ruble fell to a new low of 54.91 to the U.S. dollar Wednesday before recovering some ground. WSJ's Andrey Ostroukh and Chiara Albanese write:\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eliminated regular \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after spending nearly $30 billion of its reserves did little to stop the decline [in the ruble]. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said it reserved the right to carry out sudden \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any level to ensure financial stability and avoid panic. On Wednesday, \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  revealed that it had sold $700 million earlier in the week in defense of the ruble, which has been hitting record lows daily.\par \par \uc2 Hedge funds focused on Russia are down an average of 12% net of fees, according a CNBC in a story on emerging market hedge fund performance. But why buy a hedge fund? Bears on Russia would have done well to hold the Direxion Daily Russia Bear 3X Shares ETF ( RUSS), which is up 86% year to date, and up 89% just in the past three months. The Market Vectors Russia ETF ( RSX) has fallen nearly 34% this year. (The story notes that hedge funds invested in India were among the most stellar hedge fund performers this year, up about 42%, net of fees, though it fails to mention India small-cap ETFs did even better, up more than 56%.) See " Best Hedge Fund Bet of 2014 Is ... India?" on CNBC.com.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Murmansk, Russian prostitutes are hiking prices by 40% due to the depreciation of the ruble, the BBC reports. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Barron's Emerging Markets blog,  \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/ }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 03, 2014 18:58 ET (23:58 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141204eac30028e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
