\par\par \b \uc2 BREAKINGVIEWS-Sinking rouble puts debt squeeze on Russia Inc\b0\par\par\uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2014\par 12:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds RIC) (The author is a Reuters Breakingviews columnist. The opinions expressed are his own.)\par \par \uc2 By Pierre Brian\u231\'00\'E7on\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 3 (Reuters Breakingviews) - Russia does not have an external debt problem. At around 37 percent of GDP - versus 1.5 to three times GDP, say, for developed European economies - it should be easily manageable. For Russian companies and banks, it's a different story.\par \par \uc2 A 40 percent drop in crude oil prices in a year, a similar drop in the rouble, and the country's financial isolation due to Western sanctions are threatening Russian companies and banks with a serious debt squeeze. The state will have to step in. And that will come at a price - even greater meddling, and for some even re-nationalisation.\par \par \uc2 Russia has to service $30 billion of debt this December, then $138 billion in the subsequent 18 months, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Russia\uc2 . A paltry 2 percent of that amount is owed by the government itself. Non-financial companies account for more than 60 percent of the total, while most of the rest weighs on banks, including state-owned \uc2 Sberbank\uc2 , the country's largest lender.\par \par \uc2 Moscow isn't nearing default. And companies have some cash on hand, even though their debt in dollar terms has risen more than 60 percent since the beginning of the year. In theory some of them can benefit from the rouble's devaluation, which makes Russian exports more competitive. But exporters of non-oil products are few and far between, so the positive impact of devaluation is in fact limited.\par \par \uc2 Russian banks, on the other hand, are about to hit a steep dollar wall. They have to refinance $50 billion by mid-2016. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it has $420 billion worth of foreign reserves. That could be used to fend off a major disaster, but the CBR is also trying to limit liquidity injections into the banking system, which it suspects of speculating on the rouble's fall.\par \par \uc2 Part of those reserves is the $170 billion parked in the Russian government's two rainy-day funds. But some of that money seems to be already committed, limiting the cash on hand.\par \par \uc2 The Russian government has hinted that it can endure another two years of sanctions. The falls of oil and the rouble are shrinking that horizon by the day.\par \par \uc2 \f2               \par               \par               \par               \par CONTEXT NEWS\par \par               \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - The rouble fell 2 percent in early trading on Dec. 3 before firming up.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - The Russian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was up 1.1 percent against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's dollar-euro reference basket by 1130 GMT. It is down 35 percent since the beginning of the year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Russia must pay back or refinance $169 billion of its $731 billion total foreign debt by mid-2016, according to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  numbers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Reuters: Rouble slide resumes after c.bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - For previous columns by the author, Reuters customers can click on\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by George Hay and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sarah Bailey\f28 \uc2 \f2 )\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (On \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/pierrebri"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/pierrebri}}}\uc2 \f2 )\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-6T11:45:34.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141203eac300dkx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
