\par\par \b \uc2 Russian cenbank "undoubtedly"  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  again to defend rouble - traders\b0\par\par\uc2 122 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2014\par 11:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Dec 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market again to defend the rouble, three traders told Reuters following sharp swings in the rouble's exchange rate on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "Without doubt, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling (foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ). The whole question is what volumes it is limiting itself too," said a trader at a large Western bank in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had made $700 million in market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, its first \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Nov. 10, the day before it floated the rouble. (Reporting by Vladimir Abramov, writing by Jason Bush, editing by Timothy Heritage)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-6T10:40:30.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141203eac300eyx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
