\par\par \b \uc2 Renewed Slide in Oil Price Hits Russian Ruble Again\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh And Chiara Albanese   \par \uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2014\par 14:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 A calm spell for the Russian ruble early on Tuesday proved short-lived, with a renewed slide in oil hitting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  once more, despite the country's finance minister saying that the ruble is now too cheap.\par \par \uc2 The ruble dropped about 2.4% against the dollar, taking the dollar to 52.90 rubles. The ruble sank to a record low of 53.95 against the dollar on Monday, hit by the recent slump in oil prices which will pinch Russia's commodity-dependent budget.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister \uc2 Anton Siluanov\uc2  told reporters on Tuesday that the ruble is undervalued.\par \par \uc2 "According to finance ministry estimates, the current [ruble] rate matches an oil price of substantially below $60 per barrel. With oil at $80 per barrel an equilibrium [dollar] rate will be below 45 rubles in 2015," Mr. Siluanov said.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude was recently trading at $71.69 per barrel, down 1.2% on the day.\par \par \uc2 The combined effect of lower oil prices, geopolitical tensions and sanctions imposed against Russia are cranking up the pressure on the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which Monday fell about 6% against the dollar in a single day, the worst session since the 1998 financial crisis. Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to prop up the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The kind of crazy intraday moves we saw Monday would be fully consistent with \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reduce excessive volatility," said Ivan Tchakarov, \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 . "I find it hard to see the ruble going stronger without an attendant move up in oil prices," he added.\par \par \uc2 Adding to the pressure, this month Russian banks and companies will have to pay back around $30 billion in foreign debt, increasing the domestic demand for dollars.\par \par \uc2 Looking ahead, the market will be closely watching President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's annual state of the nation address on Thursday for his assessment of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  situation and the Ukraine crisis.\par \par \uc2 The ruble is the second worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, after Ukraine's hryvnia, having underperformed other oil \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Nigerian naira.\par \par \uc2 Ben Edwards contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com and Chiara Albanese at chiara.albanese@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 02-12-14 1309GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020141202eac2000e9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
