\par\par \b \uc2 Fed\uc2  Patience Expected as Short-End Yields Decline -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 2014\par 16:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 10:47 EST - Yields on shorter-dated Treasurys, the most sensitive to the \uc2 Fed\uc2 's rate outlook, are falling at a faster pace today than those on longer-dated bonds. Lower energy prices and a mixed global growth outlook have boosted investors' expectations that the \uc2 Fed\uc2  may wait until late 2015 if not later to raise interest rates. The odds of a rate increase at the September 2015 FOMC last at 41%, down from 49% at the end of last week and 56% a month ago. Two-year notes up 2/32, yielding 0.465%. The five-year note is the best performer, up 5/32 to yield 1.476%. (min.zeng@wsj.com; @minzengwsj)\par \par \uc2 10:38 EST - Soybean futures traded in Chicago will decline 8% through 2015 because of rising global stockpiles, increasing plantings and declining biodiesel production, agricultural lender \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  says. Global supplies have significantly improved thanks to this year's expected record US crop, and the firm expects Brazil's output to rise 7% next year to a record 92M metric tons. \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  sees Q1 2015 soy futures at $9.70/bushel. It also predicts lower daily price volatility due to improved global supplies. One wild card: how much US farmers switch to planting soybeans from more costly-to-produce corn next spring. \uc2 CBOT\uc2  January soybeans unchanged at $10.16/bushel. (david.kesmodel@wsj.com; @davidkesmodel)\par \par \uc2 1537 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--To profit from the limited \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite the freefall of the ruble, \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  recommends a long spot position in TRY/RUB, currently trading at 23.5729. "We target a 8% move higher to 25.4587, and place a stop-loss at 22.6300," says the bank. Given the extremely elevated intra-day volatility, strategists caution to only place a small allocation to the trade which would have a trade horizon of approximately 1 month. (chiara.albanese@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10:26 EST - Brazilian soy farmers have planted 85% of the area they plan to sow with the crop, according to the Safras & Mercado consultancy. In Mato Grosso state, Brazil's biggest soy producer with about 30% of the total crop, planting is almost finished, with 98% done, and in the second-biggest soy producing state, Parana, it was 96% finished, Safras said. A lack of rain in northern and northeastern states has slowed planting in that region, but even there it should be finished by Dec. 21, the consultancy said. (jeffrey.lewis@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10:21 EST - The ISM's input prices index plunges to 44.5 in November from 53.5 in October. The ISM says it's the first time raw materials prices have posted a decline since July 2013. The drop in energy prices is the main cause. Among the commodities down in price are crude oil, gasoline and other oil-based products. (kathleen.madigan@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10:18 EST - A November drop for a Midwest business index signals slower economic gains ahead as lower crop and energy prices weigh on the region. The Mid-America Business Conditions Index, which tracks economic activity in a 9-state region from North Dakota to Arkansas, fell to 51.3 from 51.8 in October. "While I still expect positive growth, it will be down from the same period for 2013," says Creighton University professor Ernie Goss, who oversees the index. "Growth in urban areas of the region" will outpace nonurban locales "in the months ahead." (mark.peters@wsj.com; @mrmmpeters)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1517 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Russia's government is far from introducing capital controls in response to the ruble weakening, \f28 \uc2 \f2 ING\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Egor Fedorov says, but adds "somewhere a thin red line exists, when old books on capital control will be opened and tough decisions will be made." Notes any hints from the government side on a possibility of an introduction of a capital control will lead to a further ruble sell off. (alexander.kolyandr@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10:17 EST - The ISM manufacturing PMI eases only a bit in November, falling to 58.7 from 59.0 in October. New orders rise to 66.0 and even exports orders pop up last month. Solid demand is helping production and employment. The ISM says comments show manufacturers are upbeat. The main worry: "West Coast port slowdowns and the threat of a potential dock strike." (kathleen.madigan@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10:15 EST - The dollar gets a boost after the US ISM November manufacturing read comes in above market forecasts at 58.7, signaling the US economy remains on relatively strong footing. The numbers arrive ahead of a heavy week of market indicators that are expected to provide direction for investors. The dollar climbs to Y118.21 from Y117.93 ahead of the numbers, but remains down 0.3% versus the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The euro loses some earlier gains against the greenback, declining to $1.2487 from $1.2500 beforehand, but still up 0.3%. (james.ramage@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1512 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 AXA Investment\f28 \uc2 \f2  Managers has reorganised its fixed income and structured finance teams and created a new fixed income and structured finance department, the company said. \f28 \uc2 \f2 John Porter\f28 \uc2 \f2 , global head of the team will oversee the department. "The new arrangement provides a simpler structure [and] will facilitate the integration of structured finance assets into traditional fixed income so that \f28 \uc2 \f2 AXA\f28 \uc2 \f2  IM can offer solutions which address changing client needs across the credit spectrum," the asset manager said. (chiara.albanese@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1511 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The ruble's exchange rate of 50 to 52 per dollar is "fundamentally justified" at the current oil prices, Dmitri Petrov from Nomura says, adding the bouncing back of the ruble in the past hours was due to the "markets losing confidence in their short positions," rather than the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . He doesn't see a level at which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  feels obliged to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , rather it may react to the speed of the decline. (alexander.kolyandr@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10:10 EST - Since joining the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  in June, Lael Brainard has been silent in her public role as a governor. That changes this week when the official will speak three times. Her key addresses are on Wednesday and Thursday--both on financial stability issues. Those two events in Washington will help the public get a better understanding of where Brainard stands on what's become the de facto third mandate for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . It's also a big week for \f28 \uc2 \f2 New York Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  leader \f28 \uc2 \f2 William Dudley\f28 \uc2 \f2 , who speaks on the economy and monetary policy today and tours the Bronx on Tuesday. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  Vice Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Stanley Fischer\f28 \uc2 \f2  is also on the stump today on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  history, followed by remarks later in the week. (michael.derby@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 01, 2014 10:47 ET (15:47 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141201eac10026o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
