\par\par \uc2 Top Stories\par \b \uc2 Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Props Up Ruble\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh \par \uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 2014\par 14:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top North American Equities Stories\par \uc2 DJTNAE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Monday to prop up the ruble after it staged a biggest one-day drop since 1998, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "It is likely that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by placing orders to sell dollars at lower and lower levels," said Pavel Demeshchik, a trader at ING Bank in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 "We are making this conclusion, judging by the style of how that was made. It is unlikely that any other player [apart from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] is intended to behave in such manner," Mr. Demeshchik said.\par \par \uc2 Hit by a drop in oil prices, the ruble weakened to a fresh record low of 53.95 against the dollar by 1147 GMT, but then recovered to 51.9 to the greenback in less than 30 minutes.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  let the ruble float freely in early November, but warned that it retains the right to carry out sudden \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any level if it deems its necessary for financial stability, or to prevent households from panic ditching of rubles. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and only reveals its trading activity on its website with a two-day lag.\par \par \uc2 "It looked like a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today," said Dmitry Stadnik, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Rosbank, the Russian subsidiary of French bank Societe Generale.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Stadnik said that some market participant was putting orders on the Moscow exchange to sell dollars in amounts from $150 million to $200 million at around 20 kopecks below the actual market price.\par \par \uc2 Market participants on the Moscow exchange can see prices of a deal and sometimes the volume, but not the name of the transaction party.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJTNAE1120141201eac10003d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
