\par\par \uc2 Top Stories\par \b \uc2 OPEC Decision, Oil Prices Continue to Hit Oil-linked Stocks,  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By JOSIE COX and CHIARA ALBANESE \par \uc2 756 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2014\par 18:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top Energy Stories\par \uc2 DJTES\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The tumbling price of oil hammered commodity-dependent \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as shares in oil and gas companies Friday, a day after the Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries left its output target unchanged, diminishing hope of any imminent respite for the ailing commodity.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude was an additional 0.6% lower at $72.17 a barrel, its weakest level in four years, having already plummeted nearly 7% on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "It's really a chaotic situation and anyone's guess how far oil might still go," said James Sutton, global natural resources equity strategist at J.P. Morgan Asset Management, which looks after around $1.7 trillion worth of assets.\par \par \uc2 The sell-off in oil-related stocks continued in the U.S., where markets reopened Friday after the Thanksgiving holiday there. Oil majors like Exxon Mobil Corp. and drillers such as Transocean Ltd. were feeling the pressure.\par \par \uc2 "In recent weeks we have reduced our exposure to energy and increased our cash holdings and certainly won't be comfortable deploying that cash again before we see some kind of equilibrium returning to the market," Mr. Sutton said.\par \par \uc2 Analysts had estimated OPEC would need to take 1 million to 1.5 million barrels a day off the market to support oil prices, which have fallen by more than 30% since the summer, but its members didn't bow to market pressure.\par \par \uc2 Russia's ruble, which this year has also been pummeled by geopolitical tensions and resulting sanctions, hit yet another all-time low against the dollar, while fellow oil-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Canadian dollar, Norway's krone and Nigeria's naira slipped too.\par \par \uc2 One dollar now buys more close to 50 rubles. It started the year around 32.\par \par \uc2 "OPEC yesterday delivered just about the most unfriendly possible response to ruble and oil prices," Tom Levinson, a strategist at Sberbank said. He added that it was unclear whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide.\par \par \uc2 "[That will] be dictated by the bank's judgment of whether "financial stability" is at risk. It is hard to argue that it is not, but the hurdle to ad hoc \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has proven high to date," Mr. Levinson said.\par \par \uc2 Barclays economists said they now expect Brent crude to sink below $70 a barrel and the West Texas Intermediate benchmark to fall even further.\par \par \uc2 "Over the course of the coming months, oil markets will have to find a new equilibrium--a world where demand elasticities are tested, and non-OPEC supply sensitivities, and particularly the pain threshold for U.S. producers becomes better understood," they wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 Turkey, a major oil importer, is a bright spot. Aberdeen Asset Management said it is now taking a more favorable view of the country by buying the Turkish lira.\par \par \uc2 "There can be a shift from oil-exporter countries, we are already witnessing it in Latin America's weaker growth performance. But on a macro scale, lower energy prices should help global growth, and this should have an overall positive impact on emerging markets," said Viktor Szabo, a portfolio manager at the firm, which manages around GBP322.5 billion ($402 billion) in assets.\par \par \uc2 Istanbul's main stock exchange rose around 1.8% on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "Given that Turkey imports more than 90% of its energy needs, low oil prices will have positive implications," said emerging market strategist Piotr Matys at Rabobank.\par \par \uc2 Shares in major airlines, including easyJet PLC, International Consolidated Airlines--owner of British Airways--and TUI Travel PLC climbed, buoyed by the prospect of cheaper fuel. The Stoxx Europe 600 index of travel and leisure stocks rose 1.4%.\par \par \uc2 "A fall in oil prices means a fall in petrol prices, a fall in transport costs, and should be treated as a tax cut for consumers," Peter Dragicevich, a strategist at Commonwealth Bank of Australia wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 Retail stocks and chemical companies are also widely seen as potential beneficiaries.\par \par \uc2 But more broadly, oil and gas companies on the Stoxx Europe 600 index declined by almost 3.5% to a more than one-month low, fiercely underperforming all other sector indexes. The broader Stoxx 600 fell 0.1%.\par \par \uc2 The biggest losers on the pan-European all-share index included BG Group PLC, Petrofac Ltd., Royal Dutch Shell PLC and BP PLC.\par \par \uc2 Write to Josie Cox at josie.cox@wsj.com and Chiara Albanese at chiara.albanese@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJTES11020141128eabs0002e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
