\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. Stocks Mixed After \uc2 OPEC\uc2  Decision\b0\par\par\uc2 By Saumya Vaishampayan   \par \uc2 739 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2014\par 16:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 U.S. stocks opened mixed Friday after the \uc2 Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries\uc2  decided to maintain its oil production target.\par \par \uc2 Shares of transportation companies that benefit from lower oil prices rose, while shares of companies tied to the oil industry fell.\par \par \uc2 The Dow Jones Industrial Average rose 31 points, or 0.2%, to 17858. The S&P 500 index declined three points, or 0.1%, to 2070, while the \uc2 Nasdaq\uc2  Composite Index advanced eight points, or 0.2%, to 4796.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. stock market was closed Thursday for Thanksgiving. On Friday, it will close earlier than usual at 1 p.m. Eastern time.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 OPEC\uc2  cartel on Thursday decided to stick to its current target of producing 30 million barrels of oil a day, rejecting calls to cut output amid a steep slump in oil prices. The decision was accompanied by a commitment from \uc2 OPEC\uc2  members to comply with it. That implies a cut of around 300,000 barrels a day, based on \uc2 OPEC\uc2 's figures, since the 12-member cartel currently pumps more than its production ceiling. But that's a relatively small change in global oil supply.\par \par \uc2 Brent, the global oil benchmark, rose 1% to $73.32 a barrel. It fell 6.7% on Thursday after the \uc2 OPEC\uc2  meeting.\par \par \uc2 On the \uc2 New York Mercantile Exchange\uc2 , crude-oil futures dropped 5.8% to $69.42 a barrel. The \uc2 Nymex\uc2  floor was closed Thursday in observance of the Thanksgiving holiday, though electronic trading took place.\par \par \uc2 U.S. stocks have more than recovered from a pullback in September and October that was sparked in part by the drop in oil prices and concerns about the pace of global growth. The \uc2 Dow\uc2  closed at its 30th record on Wednesday, while the \uc2 S&P\uc2  notched its 47th closing high. Gains in recent weeks have been fueled by improving U.S. economic data and the third-quarter earnings season, which was broadly upbeat.\par \par \uc2 Many investors say falling oil prices will benefit U.S. consumers, who will begin spending more and help boost the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 "Overall, it is a net positive for the U.S., [because] we are a consumer-led economy," said Quincy Krosby, market strategist for \uc2 Prudential Financial\uc2 , referring to the \uc2 OPEC\uc2  decision.\par \par \uc2 Declines in energy stocks weighed on the S&P 500, with the sector down 5.6%. \uc2 Chevron Corp\uc2 . shares slumped 5.3% and those of \uc2 Exxon Mobil Corp\uc2 . lost 3.3%, leading declines on the \uc2 Dow\uc2  industrials.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 OPEC\uc2  decision and lower oil prices could lead to more deal activity in the energy sector, said Ms. Krosby of \uc2 Prudential Financial\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 Southwest Airlines Co\uc2 . and \uc2 Delta Air Lines Inc\uc2 ., which stand to benefit from lower oil prices, rose the most on the S&P 500.\par \par \uc2 Russia's ruble, which this year has been pummeled by geopolitical tensions and resulting sanctions, hit yet another all-time low against the dollar, while fellow oil-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Canadian dollar, Norway's krone and Nigeria's naira slipped too.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 OPEC\uc2  yesterday delivered just about the most unfriendly possible response to [the] ruble and oil prices," said Tom Levinson, a strategist at \uc2 Sberbank\uc2 . He added that it was unclear whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide.\par \par \uc2 European stock indexes were broadly lower, with the Stoxx Europe 600 down 0.3%. Data released Friday showed the eurozone's annual rate of inflation in November fell further below the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of just under 2%.\par \par \uc2 In other commodity markets, gold futures fell 1.5% to $1179.20 an ounce.\par \par \uc2 Demand for government debt increased, sending the yield on the 10-year \uc2 Treasury\uc2  note down to 2.214%. Yields fall as prices rise.\par \par \uc2 Josie Cox and Chiara Albanese contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Saumya Vaishampayan at saumya.vaishampayan@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 Access Investor Kit for \uc2 Prudential Financial, Inc\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US7443201022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US7443201022}}}\par \par \uc2 Access Investor Kit for \uc2 Southwest Airlines Co\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US8447411088"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US8447411088}}}\par \par \uc2 Access Investor Kit for \uc2 Prudential Financial, Inc\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US7443201022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US7443201022}}}\par \par \uc2 Access Investor Kit for \uc2 Southwest Airlines Co\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US8447411088"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US8447411088}}}\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 28-11-14 1512GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020141128eabs000aw\par }\page {\par