\par\par \b \uc2 Mild Weather Main Reason for French Spending Drop -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,471 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2014\par 10:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0903 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--French consumer spending was hit hard by warm weather in October. Overall, spending was down 0.9% month on month. But most of that came from a 6% slump in energy spending. Spending on clothes was up 3.4%, autos +0.2% and total manufactured goods spending edged up 0.1% on the month and 0.4% on the year.(william.horobin@dowjones.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 0902 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--From an inflation perspective, this drop in oil prices is more relevant for the ECB than other central banks, as the ECB target rate includes energy prices, says Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ. "Energy makes up a little less than 10% of the euro-zone \uc2 CPI\uc2  basket and now Brent crude oil is now down around 35% on an annual basis. If this drop is sustained through the remainder of the year, energy inflation is set to become a bigger drag on overall inflation. The annual rate is currently at -2.0% as of October and this could drop to -4.0/4.5% over the coming months," he adds. (josie.cox@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0858 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Hungary's August-October average unemployment rate was 7.1%, data published Thursday showed, lower than expected and surprising Raiffeisen Bank. The low reading was mainly due to the government's widening subsidy-for-work program, Raiffeisen notes. Warns that if the jobless rate were adjusted to this public work program, it would stand around 11.5%, a much more striking figure. (veronika.gulyas@wsj.com; @VeronikaGulyas1) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0857 GMT 0000 GMT (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow\f28 \uc2 \f2  JOnes) --Even if Swiss voters back the gold initiative Sunday, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  will certainly defend its cap of 1.20 francs per euro, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "Any attempts to speculate on the EUR/CHF level of 1.2000 being breached are likely to fail miserably, as the demands of the gold initiative wouldn't be implemented immediately," says analyst Thu Lan Nguyen. The SNB would have five years to lift its gold asset share to 20% and thus it's "neither courageous nor particularly clever to be betting on a breach of the minimum exchange rate now," he notes. The EUR/CHF was last at 1.2020. (neil.maclucas@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0857 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Revised Czech 3Q GDP readings bode well for the country's economic recovery, providing there is no major slowdown in Germany. "The main risk for our economic growth outlook of 2.6% in 2014 and 2.4% in 2015 weould be a more profound growth weakening in Germany and other key European economies," says Raiffeisenbank economist Helena Horska. Another round of economic sanctions against Russia and the halt of Siberian gas supplies to Europe also pose potential risks, she says. The revised 3Q GDP data show the Czech economy expanded 0.4% on quarterly and 2.4% on annual terms. "This improves the overall Czech economic picture," Horska says. (leos.rousek@wsj.com, @LeoRousek) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0854 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Bonds issued by Russian firms and banks are under pressure Friday as oil prices continue to slide after \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  members said they wouldn't cut supply. Yield spreads on bonds from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2  to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sberbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  are wider from 5 bps to as much as around 60 bps, Tradeweb data show. Bonds from Russian firms have already been hit hard this year after Europe and the U.S. slapped sanctions on certain Russian borrowers in response to the violence in eastern Ukraine. Lower oil prices will further weigh on Russia's economic outlook. (ben.edwards@wsj.com @debtnerd) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0848 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--"\f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  yesterday delivered just about the most unfriendly possible response to ruble and oil prices, essentially abdicating its role as chief global swing producer," strategists at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sberbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  write in a note. "Whether or not [the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in huge amounts will be dictated by its judgment of whether 'financial stability' is at risk. It is hard to argue that it is not, but the hurdle to ad hoc \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has proven high to date," they add. (josie.cox@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0833 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  economists say there's a two-thirds likelihood that the ECB will take the plunge into large-scale government bond purchases, or "quantitative easing." They say that ECB president \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mario Draghi\f28 \uc2 \f2 's speech one week ago "made it clear that the ECB is not willing to tolerate an inflation rate that is much too low for comfort. Also, the ECB knows that the markets would react negatively if QE did not take place," they said. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says it thinks that the ECB will likely embark on QE at one of its first three meetings next year. (todd.buell@wsj.com) (@ToddBuell) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0830 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  (7203.TO) parts-making affiliate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aisin Seiki\f28 \uc2 \f2  (7259.TO) close up 4.2% at Y4,245, while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyota\f28 \uc2 \f2  adds 2.3% to Y7,314 following a Nikkei report that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  group will integrate braking system \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at Aisin subsidiary Advics, and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Denso\f28 \uc2 \f2  (6902.TO). \f28 \uc2 \f2 Denso\f28 \uc2 \f2  also added 1.1% to Y5,543. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyota\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to transfer development and production of its braking systems to Advics as early as next year, the report said; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyota\f28 \uc2 \f2  owns a 22% stake in both \f28 \uc2 \f2 Denso\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aisin Seiki\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "The move appears to be a natural progression for two of the world's top auto parts makers," said SMBC Nikko Securities senior analyst Kunihiro Matsumoto. "There should be room for synergistic mid-term growth." (bradford.frischkorn@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: ALP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0828 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The Loonie suffered Thursday post-OPEC, however \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  remains upbeat on Canada's domestic outlook. The bank says the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is particularly sensitive to any upside data surprises following the very strong October \f28 \uc2 \f2 CPI\f28 \uc2 \f2  print, which calls into question just how long the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2  can remain neutral going forward. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  survey forecast for September monthly GDP is +0.4% vs -0.1% in August, data out 1330 GMT. USD/CAD now 1.1380. gary.stride@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0827 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Hong Kong equities bifurcate in the afternoon session as investors chase the biggest weekly rally in the Shanghai Composite in more than four years. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Seng\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index slides 0.1% to 23,987.45, while the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Seng\f28 \uc2 \f2 China Enterprises\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index surges 1.2% to 11,145.39, capping its weekly gain at 6.8% -- the biggest in more than a year. "The plunge in oil is obviously bad for all the energy companies and alternatives like shale oil, but it acts like a massive tax cut for Asia and opens the door for more easing across the region with inflation continuing to moderate. Don't fight the central banks," says David Welch, head of equity sales trading at Reorient Group. "Investors are massively underweight China and are scrambling to catch up; insurance were the first movers but now it's time for the banks to rally as newsflow is getting much better." (Gregor.Hunter@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: ALP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0823 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Bad loans at Indian state-run banks could increase as a result of the cancellation of coal-mining licenses. The cancellations may impact the $15.5 billion of loans extended by state-run banks to power plants, which are facing a shortage of coal--their key input--and may have to stop generating bioelectricity as a result, junior finance minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jayant Sinha\f28 \uc2 \f2  told the lower house of Parliament. India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Supreme Court\f28 \uc2 \f2  cancelled 204 licenses in September after it termed the previous government process of allotment of the licenses as ambiguous and arbitrary. It directed the government to develop a transparent process for allocation of the mineral resource. State-run banks' bad loans are at 0.23% of their total advances to coal industry. (prasanta.sahu@wsj.com, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @pksahu9) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: ALP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 28, 2014 04:03 ET (09:03 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141128eabs000pt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
