\par\par \b \uc2 EARNINGS POLL-\uc2 Vimpelcom\uc2  3rd qtr profit, sales seen hit by  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  loss\b0\par\par\uc2 485 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2014\par 12:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vimpelcom\f28 \uc2 \f2  Q3 results\par     * Due on Wednesday, Nov. 12\par     * Net profit seen down 16 pct\par \par     MOSCOW, Nov 11 (Reuters) - Amsterdam-based international mobile operator\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vimpelcom\f28 \uc2 \f2  is expected to report on Wednesday a 16 percent decline in\par third-quarter net income and lower revenue, hit by the devaluation of the rouble\par and Ukrainian hryvnia, a Reuters poll showed.\par     The average forecast of three analysts surveyed in a Reuters poll was a net\par profit of around $213 million taking into account likely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par losses, down from $255 million a year ago. The other seven banks surveyed by\par Reuters forecast an average $359 million net profit before \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses.\par     "We expect an increase in depreciation on higher investments but expect\par interest costs to decline following the refinancing earlier this year. At the\par same time, we expect a fairly large \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loss, which is why we estimate\par earnings to decline by 36 percent year-on-year to $164 million," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par     The rouble has slumped over 25 percent against the dollar this year as\par plunging oil prices and Western sanctions over Ukraine have shrivelled Russia's\par exports and investment inflows. Last week, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Russia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  effectively\par abandoned the trading corridor for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , halting the multi-billion\par dollar daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that had propped it up. \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is the biggest market for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vimpelcom\f28 \uc2 \f2  which also has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par several other former Soviet republics including Ukraine, as well as in Italy,\par Algeria, Bangladesh, and Pakistan.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vimpelcom\f28 \uc2 \f2 's revenue and core profit, or EBITDA, were seen falling 11 percent\par and 14 percent respectively, also hit by weaker revenue and rising costs in\par Ukraine as well as increased network rollout expenses in Africa and Asia.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vimpelcom\f28 \uc2 \f2 , in which Russia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alfa Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Norway's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telenor\f28 \uc2 \f2  are\par the biggest shareholders, had said it expected "low to mid single digit"\par declines in sales and EBITDA. \par     Following is a summary of forecasts for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vimpelcom\f28 \uc2 \f2 's results (figures in\par millions of dollars unless otherwise stated):    \par               Revenue    EBITDA*  EBITDA margin  Net profit  Adj. net profit**  \par   \par  Average       5,065      2,125      42.0%         213.3          358.9  \par  High          5,120      2,160      42.4%         278.0          452.0   \par  Low           5,032      2,088      41.2%         164.0          259.0\par  Median        5,057      2,126      42.0%         198.0          344.0   \par  No of fcsts***   10         10        10              3              7    \par  Q3 2013       5,685      2,474      43.5%         255.0            N/A    \par  Q2 2014       5,067      2,076      41.0%         100.0            N/A\par     \par  * Earnings before interest, taxation, depreciation and amortisation.\par  ** Adjusted for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses stemming from the devaluation of\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vimpelcom\f28 \uc2 \f2 's operating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , mainly the rouble, against the dollar. \par  *** Forecasts provided by: Citi, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2 ,\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Otkritie, Raiffeisen Research, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sberbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Uralsib, and VTB\par Capital.\par \par  (Reporting by Maria Kiselyova; editing by Susan Thomas)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-14T11:23:24.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141111eabb00b9m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
