\par\par \b \uc2 El-Arian: Russia Is Losing Control -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dimitra DeFotis   \par \uc2 461 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2014\par 19:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Russia appears to be losing control of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the face of a potential financial crisis, says Mohamed El-Arian.\par \par \uc2 The Market Vectors Russia ETF ( RSX) is down 1% today. U.S.-traded \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shares of   \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sberbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  ( SBRCY), the state-run lender targeted by international sanctions, and natural gas producer  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2  ( OGZPY), are each down 2%. Shares of Norisk Nickel Mining and Metallurgical ( NILSY) are down 1.3%. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Among more volatile trading vehicles focused on Russia, the Direxion Daily Russia Bear 3X Shares ETF ( RUSS) is up 3.3 today, while the Direxion Daily Russia Bull 3X Shares ETF ( RUSL) is down 3%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 El-Arian, the chief economic advisor at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Allianz\f28 \uc2 \f2  who left PIMCO earlier this year, writes in his latest Bloomberg column that "something will have to give in the next few weeks:"\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The [Russian] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's retreat from propping up the ruble highlights the fix the country is in. The authorities' initial response was to use ample international reserves to counter the impact of sanctions imposed by the West after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's actions in Ukraine. They backed this up by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and repo markets, which readily exchange securities for cash, and by raising interest rates. This moderated what would have been more disorderly pressures on the ruble and an even faster loss of confidence. But the subsequent collapse in oil prices and the pickup in capital flight overwhelmed this strategy, forcing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week to retreat from its policy and fully float the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Something will have to give in the next few weeks. The country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  situation could spin further out of control, at one extreme, or the Russian authorities might respond strongly with a range of fiscal and monetary measures, on the other, including higher interest rates and spending cuts. Either approach would risk depressing economic activity even more in the short run. ..."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 See " Ruble Rebound Bolsters Russian Stocks," by Barron's Randall Forsyth and " How Close Is Russia To Financial Crisis?" by El-Arian on Bloomberg. Also see " Can Russian Woes Hammer the U.S. Stock Market?" (subscription required) by Barron's John Kimelman.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Kremlin published a Putin Q&A, in English, from this week's APEC CEO Summit in China that addresses Russia's desire to drum up investment and boost energy deals with China. What got as much attention: Putin's chivalry, rebuffed: censors buried images showing Russia's leader placing a shawl on the shoulders of China's first lady at an event, \f28 \uc2 \f2 CNN\f28 \uc2 \f2  reports. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Barron's Emerging Markets blog, \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 11, 2014 13:23 ET (18:23 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141111eabb002rp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
