\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Interventions \highlight\uc2  Needed To Stop Ruble's Decline, Says Julius Baer -- Market\b0\par\par\uc2 166 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2014\par 15:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1415 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--To stop the decline of the ruble, either higher interest rates or \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells U.S. dollars and buys rubles are needed, says David Kohl, economist at Julius Baer. He expects the ruble to weaken to 50 against the dollar in 12 months. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduce the amount of rubles in \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and have hence a very similar tightening effect on the economy to higher interest rates," he says. While so far Russia holds sufficient funds to avoid a full-blown crisis the risk that drastic measures like capital controls are necessary to avoid further escalation is rising, which would weigh on sentiment of emerging market investments in general, he says. USD/RUB trades at 46.69. (chiara.albanese@wsj.com @chiaraalbanese)\par \par \uc2 Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464\par \par \uc2 markettalk@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 11-11-14 1432GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020141111eabb000ar\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
