\par\par \b \uc2 European Markets, Ruble Higher-- 3rd Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Josie Cox   \par \uc2 836 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2014\par 19:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 European markets rose Monday, shrugging off news that over two million Catalans had voted overwhelmingly in favor of independence, defying a Spanish court.\par \par \uc2 Pro-independence Catalans pointed to the high turnout at the vote over the weekend, despite legal and logistical hurdles, to bolster their case to be permitted to hold a formal, binding referendum--akin to the one held in Scotland in September--on separating their wealthy region from Spain.\par \par \uc2 But Spain's IBEX stock index took the news in its stride, closing 1.3% higher, while the yield on the 10-year Spanish bond was also steady at 2.124%.\par \par \uc2 "Markets should treat this calmly, as the constitutional position in Catalonia is very different from that of, say, Scotland in September," said Paul Donovan, an economist at \uc2 UBS\uc2 . \uc2 Alberto Gallo\uc2 , head of macro credit research at \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2 , agreed.\par \par \uc2 "Although headline political risks remain, we expect the vote result to have a limited impact on Spanish spreads," he said.\par \par \uc2 "The most likely outcome is a more prolonged negotiation in 2015, possibly resulting in some delegation of political or economic powers to Catalonia," he added, confirming his positive view on Spanish credit.\par \par \uc2 The Stoxx Europe 600 ended the session 0.7% higher, recouping Friday's 0.5% decline that was prompted by a lukewarm jobs report from the U.S. and some investors taking profits on sharp gains after the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday said it plans to massively expand its balance sheet.\par \par \uc2 In the U.S., the S&P 500 was up 0.2% in late European trade, while the Dow Jones Industrial Average climbed 0.1%.\par \par \uc2 In terms of company stock moves in Europe, shares in the U.K.'s \uc2 Serco Group PLC\uc2  were notable underperformers of the day.\par \par \uc2 The company, which provides outsource services to governments, such as managing the custody of prisoners, saw its shares plummeted 32% to the bottom of the Stoxx Europe 600, after the firm cut its full-year financial guidance and said it plans to raise GBP550 million ($873.2 million) in a rights issue next year. It said that it had identified GBP1.5 billion of likely impairments and charges.\par \par \uc2 "There is a lot to absorb today, but it is important to note this might not be the end of the bad news and that any turnaround is going to be a long process," said Andrew Gibb, an equity analyst at Investec.\par \par \uc2 Shares in peer \uc2 G4S PLC\uc2  slipped on the news too, while the \uc2 FTSE\uc2  350 Support Services index of the 33 biggest firms in the sector in the U.K. shed 0.2%, underperforming the \uc2 FTSE\uc2  100 all-sector index which rose 0.7%.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, Russia's ruble leapt higher Monday, following its recent record-breaking drubbing, gaining strength after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterated that it stands ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any time.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell by over 2.2% to 45.65 against the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  dismissed its drop in recent days as "speculative" and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was cutting ruble supply to stem speculative pressure.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said that it would eliminate the trading corridor it has been setting and the regular \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reached those boundaries. However, it said it would still \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it sees "threats to financial stability."\par \par \uc2 That helped \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Micex stock index to add 1.2%, and the dollar-denominated RTS index to rise 3.75%, but some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists warned against becoming too optimistic too soon.\par \par \uc2 "We are seeing some relief in the short-term, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is certainly not out of the woods," said Piotr Matys, an emerging market strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 . The ruble has lost almost 40% against the U.S. dollar since the start of the year and around 5.5% since the start of November.\par \par \uc2 In Ukraine, meanwhile, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said that it would consider further measures to support its plunging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the hryvnia, if it doesn't stabilize in the coming days. The hryvnia was 2.3% lower against the dollar Monday and is down 45% so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were calm, with the euro steady at $1.244 while the yen was slightly stronger at Yen114.66 against the dollar, which some attributed to the slightly softer-than-expected U.S. payroll reading on Friday.\par \par \uc2 In commodity markets, Brent crude resumed its fall and was down 1% at $82.65 at the close, having earlier in the session rebounded after China's trade data showed imports of crude oil rose 18.0% year-over-year in October, compared with a 7.4% year-over-year rise in September. Gold also ended the day 1% lower at $1,157.80 per troy ounce.\par \par \uc2 Write to Josie Cox at josie.cox@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 10, 2014 13:03 ET (18:03 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141110eaba003c1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
