\par\par \b \uc2 PRESS DIGEST - RUSSIA - Nov 10\b0\par\par\uc2 413 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2014\par 12:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 10 (Reuters) - The following are some of the stories in Russian newspapers on Monday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.\par \par \uc2 VEDOMOSTI\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.vedomosti.ru"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.vedomosti.ru}}}\par \par \uc2 - Russian Prime Minister \uc2 Dmitry Medvedev\uc2  is planning on Monday to look at ways of restructuring miner Mechel's debts, mainly to state-controlled banks, the newspaper says.\par \par \uc2 - Russia's \uc2 Gazprom\uc2 , Rosneft and Lukoil are considering listing securities on the Hong Kong stock exchange in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the daily says.\par \par \uc2 - The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it could increase its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "at any moment" to back up \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rouble after it collapsed to 60 roubles to the U.S. dollar on Friday.\par \par \uc2 - Rosneft and Independent Oil company could bid for shares of \uc2 Bashneft\uc2  after the government succeeded in reclaiming control over the company, the daily says. A Moscow court last week ordered the seizure of a more than 70 percent stake that belonged to the conglomerate controlled by wealthy businessman Vladimir Yevtushenkov.\par \par \uc2 KOMMERSANT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.kommersant.ru"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.kommersant.ru}}}\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Gazprom\uc2 's South Stream pipeline project to Europe has lost its main importance for the company after \uc2 Gazprom\uc2 's chief, \uc2 Alexei Miller\uc2 , signed a framework agreement on Sunday on launching gas supplies to China, the daily says.\par \par \uc2 - Russian lawyers believe the Moscow arbitration court's decision to back the return of shares in \uc2 Bashneft\uc2  to the state because of violations of the privatisation rules two decades ago sets a dangerous precedent which could affect other owners of privatised assets, the daily says.\par \par \uc2 IZVESTIA\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.izvestia.ru"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.izvestia.ru}}}\par \par \uc2 - Arkady Rotenberg, a Russian businessman who has been hit by sanctions in the Ukraine crisis, is launching a new project in Russia on "construction and management of sports sites". His nephew Roman Rotenberg will head the new company, the daily reports.\par \par \uc2 - President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , recognised by Forbes as the world's most influential person this month, disapproves of the use of his name and image for commercial purposes, according to his spokesman, \uc2 Dmitry Peskov\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NEZAVISIMAYA GAZETA\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.ng.ru"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.ng.ru}}}\par \par \uc2 - Russia's human rights ombudsman, Ella Pamfilova, has failed to win President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's support in her attempt to prevent the closure of one of the oldest and most respected human rights organisations, Memorial, the daily says. It adds that the Kremlin has taken a tough position on non-government organisations and as a result refuses to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tatiana Ustinova, Editing by Timothy Heritage) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-10T12:09:25.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141110eaba00aqd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
