\par\par \b \uc2 The  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  of the Russian Federation\uc2  (Bank of Russia)-On the situation in the  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market\b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2014\par \uc2 ENP Newswire\par \uc2 ENPNEW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014, Electronic News Publishing. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 Release date - 07112014\par \par \uc2 The ruble exchange rate and its influence on the financial and real sectors of the economy have recently caused public concern.\par \par \uc2 The ruble\u8217\'20\'19s depreciation was prompted by a number of fundamental factors, first of all, by the falling price of oil and limited access to external capital markets.\par \par \uc2 In order to hamper the ruble\u8217\'20\'19s depreciation in October alone the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the amount of USD 30 billion.\par \par \uc2 The decisions taken by the Bank of Russia on 5 November 2014 to change the exchange rate policy mechanism along with a rise in the key rate and introduction of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  repos are only a part of measures aimed at ensuring financial and price stability amid new economic conditions.\par \par \uc2 Changes in the exchange rate policy are designed for the ruble to shortly reach an equilibrium value, to lower the excessive rate of reserve spending, and to prevent stable depreciation expectations amid the ongoing weakening of the ruble. Moreover, this decision will minimise the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the structural liquidity deficit. Thus, the exchange rate flexibility will make it possible to mitigate the impact of external shocks on the financial sector and the economy as a whole.\par \par \uc2 As a result of the decision taken, the exchange rate has begun to be adjusted, which is accompanied by increased volatility. The \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market adaptation to the new exchange rate policy mechanism will take some time, in the course of which the exchange rate may fluctuate in different directions.\par \par \uc2 According to Bank of Russia estimates, with due account of the measures taken and the occurred decline in the exchange rate, there is no need for the ruble to depreciate further to reach the balance of payments equilibrium.\par \par \uc2 The signs of feverish demand have been registered recently, which entails risks to financial stability. Against this backdrop the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to increase \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any moment, as well as to use other financial market instruments available.\par \par \uc2 [Editorial queries for this story should be sent to newswire@enpublishing.co.uk]\par \par \uc2 Dokument ENPNEW0020141110eaba000ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
