\par\par \b \uc2 Ukraine's  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  reserves plummet 23 percent to nine-year low\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalia Zinets and Alessandra  Prentice  \par \uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2014\par 15:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 KIEV (Reuters) - Ukraine's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves plummeted by almost a quarter month-on-month in October to $12.6 billion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday, due to energy payments and support for the faltering hryvnia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Reserves are now at their lowest level since 2005 and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which drew from its coffers to help state energy firm Naftogaz service its multi-billion dollar debt to Russia, will have to dip into them further as further payments loom.\par \par \uc2 "The dynamics (of the October fall) were influenced by the need to support Naftogaz (with) almost $2 billion ... and also by making payments for natural gas supplies from European suppliers," the bank said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 On Monday the bank said it had sold $1.3 billion in the past month and a half to defend the hryvnia, which has lost around 40 percent of its value against the dollar since the start of 2014 because of political upheaval, ongoing tension with \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a separatist conflict in eastern Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the hryvnia lost more ground this week, falling 7.8 percent to 13.96 to the dollar - its weakest since Sept. 19.\par \par \uc2 Continuing hryvnia fragility and upcoming gas payments mean the bank will have to dig even deeper into reserves soon, \uc2 Standard Bank\uc2  analyst Tim Ash said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "Ukraine still has $1.6 billion in gas debts to pay by year end, and $700 million-plus a month to pay for any gas deliveries ... foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve levels might well drop into single digits by year end, which is very, very low," he said.\par \par \uc2 RUSSIAN GAS\par \par \uc2 Last week Moscow, Kiev and the \uc2 European Union\uc2  clinched a deal in Brussels that would restart flows of Russian gas to Ukraine over the winter in return for Naftogaz paying part of its debt and $760 million up front for November supplies.\par \par \uc2 Naftogaz transferred the first $1.45 billion tranche of debt repayment to Russia's \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  on Tuesday and pledged to pay the rest according to the schedule, but it has not specified when it will start paying up front for fresh supplies.\par \par \uc2 On Friday the company received a bill for fresh flows from \uc2 Gazprom\uc2 , but Naftogaz stressed it would only announce the timing of any payment once it had made the decision to buy more gas.\par \par \uc2 "The amount and schedule of prepayment depends on what volume and when Naftogaz orders gas from \uc2 Gazprom\uc2 ," Naftogaz said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The longer Ukraine can put off ordering more Russian gas, the better for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Valeriia Gontareva said the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , which is supporting Kiev with a multi-billion-dollar loan package, had agreed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can pay for Russian gas directly from reserves.\par \par \uc2 They are likely already lower than the $12.6 billion figure given for October due to this week's $1.45 billion Naftogaz debt repayment.\par \par \uc2 The last time state dollar-funds were at this level in 2005, reserves staged a dramatic recovery, rising from $9.5 billion to $19.4 by the end of the year due to an influx of foreign investment following the 'Orange Revolution' that stoked hopes of a pro-democracy government.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by \uc2 Alison Williams\uc2  and Tom Heneghan) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-7T14:11:54.000Z  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141107eab700fti\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
