\par\par \b \uc2 Ruble Recovers; Major European Bank Seen Taking Profit -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2014\par 11:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1035 GMT The ruble hit a fresh record low of 48.65 versus the U.S. dollar in early trade on Friday but briefly recovered to 47.38. A trader at a major Moscow bank says the ruble's rebound was driven by one of the big European banks, which had been betting on the weaker ruble has now decided to lock in profits. Betting on the weaker ruble has become risky as the market awaits the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily any minute to deter speculators. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not immediately able to comment and has been keeping silence after scaling down \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  substantially on Wednesday.(andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1027 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Thailand's ability to boost its economy amid a stream of negative news and events is compared to "a sturdy ship in choppy waters" by Barnabas Gan, an economist at OCBC in Singapore. "The [Thai] economy is worthy of its coined nickname of being a 'Teflon economy', given its ability to bounce back from the ashes of political turmoil and shore up positive growth through appropriate monetary and fiscal policies," says Gan who also commends the structurally soundness of the economy, which he see carrying the nation to a robust 2015 recovery. Convinced that recent improvement in economic indicators is too late to boost growth this year, OCBC now project Thailand's gross domestic product growth of 0.0%-0.5% for 2014, but projects 4.0% growth for 2015. (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@dowjones.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1023 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Friday's ratings schedule may bring more bad news for France, at least if \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  is proved right. DBRS ratings agency is due to review France after today's market close, and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  sees an "elevated risk" of DBRS changing its outlook to negative, following similar moves by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Fitch in October. What chance an actual downgrade next year? (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1013 GMT The continued slide of the ruble is likely to force the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  into making a one-off \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market rather more quickly than it had initially hoped, says Capital Economics. Adds that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is also likely to be pushed into a further large hike in interest rates. Past form suggests that rates may need to rise to as much as 11.50%-12.00%, from 9.50% currently, Capital Economics says. The ruble is currently at 47.33 per dollar and 58.67 per euro. (Alexander.kolyandr@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1010 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Hungary's trade surplus is set to be higher this year than last year's EUR6.6 billion surplus, Erste Bank says, in light of September's figure--a historic monthly high of EUR952.7 million. September's exports were likely boosted by German luxury car maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Audi\f28 \uc2 \f2 's capacity expansion at its Hungarian plant, Erste adds. Expects exports to rise 4.2% this year, slower than a 4.4% increase it sees in imports. Household consumption recovery is boosting imports, it adds. Says the trade surplus will narrow in 2015 as domestic consumption will become the driver of GDP growth versus exports, its usual driver. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1006 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields are back at highs last seen a month ago on expectations of a better-than-expected U.S. nonfarm payrolls release. The December \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  contract is down 4/32 to 125-300, while the yield on the 10-year cash up to 2.39%. Analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  looks for nonfarm payrolls to show an increase by 240k, broadly in line with the average of the past three months and slightly above market consensus of 235k, and an unchanged unemployment rate of 5.9%. (nick.cawley@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0951 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The uptick in U.S. yields is helping to support the USD against many major and EM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , notes \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The bank says downside range breaks in EUR/USD and GBP/USD point to further weakness, with immediate targets of 1.2340 and 1.5750 respectively. Adds USD/JPY's bull-run should extend to 116.00. The U.S. 10-year yield is currently at a 1-month high of 2.39%. (gary.stride@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0948 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Indian government has begun the process for rolling out national portability of cellphone numbers across the country's 22 telecommunications service areas. The Department of Telecommunications in a note said it has given six months to all cellphone operators to keep their infrastructure ready to roll out the service. The service will allow cellphone users in India to change their operator and service area while allowing them to retain their phone number. (krishna.jai@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @jaikrishna) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0939 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/PHP is higher late Friday on the broad strength of the greenback. "The dollar was strong across the board. But many in the market are wary the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," says a local bank trade, referring to the narrow trading band. The USD/PHP close at 45.03 after settling at 45.00 on Thursday. Volume is moderate. Traders expect the USD/PHP to keep moving within the 44.80-45.20 range in the near term. (Cris.Larano@DowJones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0936 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Portugal's debt agency may announce a government bond auction any time during the day, for next Wednesday, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. If market expectations prove right and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  upgrades Portugal's rating outlook after Friday's market close, the timing would bode well as Portuguese bond auctions can be held on the second or fourth Wednesday of the month. "Interestingly, the IGCP [Portuguese debt agency] should know by the time of its [bond] supply announcement the outcome of the potential rating review to be published only after close of business," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says, adding that, even if \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  stays put, the debt agency should opt for the post-ECB and post-payrolls week to wrap up its 2014 bond funding. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0933 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China and Japan have agreed to resume diplomatic and security talks, apparently clearing the way for a meeting of the leaders of the two countries and reducing geopolitical risk. China and Japan have agreed to resume diplomatic and security talks, \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's Ministry of Foreign Affairs\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a statement released after a meeting between senior officials of the countries in Beijing. NHK reported that Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe and China's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Communist Party\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xi Jinping\f28 \uc2 \f2  are set to meet during the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation\f28 \uc2 \f2  forum in Beijing. The language was vague regarding the heart of their dispute--the East China Sea islands that both sides claim--but the fact that they have agreed on resumption of talks signals a reduction in tension for the time being. (liyan.qi@wsj.com; william.kazer@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0931 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Hungary's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mortgage loan conversion will likely take place at near market exchange rate, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says, basing its view on remarks by Hungary's Economy Minister this week. Says this step will not introduce fresh uncertainties as the government is unlikely to push banks too hard on the issue, in the wake of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Supreme Court\f28 \uc2 \f2  stating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk should essentially be borne by borrowers, not lenders. Such a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Supreme Court\f28 \uc2 \f2  opinion limits the government's room for manoeuvre, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  notes. (veronika.gulyas@wsj.com; @VeronikaGulyas1) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 07, 2014 05:35 ET (10:35 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141107eab7001qt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
